From da62a9e539a4a2e6fa7d14533433dc4fb7f1b0f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:26:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cheeseburger: CPU/GPU governor with a heat limit (boot-arg
 sweetpower=1)

Every 50 ms: CPU level from HOST_CPU_LOAD_INFO (1132.8/1728/1958.4 MHz),
GPU level from frames presented and submits (288/412.8 MHz at GX 700 mV,
508.8 MHz at 916 mV). TSENS0 gold sensors 7-10 cap the CPU at 75/85 C, GPU
sensors 12-13 cap the GPU at 85/95 C, 5 C hysteresis, unreadable = hot.
kern.sweetpower_gov turns it off and on, kern.sweetpower_temp reads heat.
Runtime GPU switches no longer measure (2 ms under the ring lock).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_a540_b.c |  24 +++-
 bsd/dev/sweet_mss.c    |   4 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_power.c  | 291 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 307 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

